{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1556421-brand-manger-jason-carl-just-left-white-wolf","id":1556421,"title":"Brand manger Jason Carl just left White Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-09T18:20:47-08:00","id":1556421,"title":"Brand manger Jason Carl just left White Wolf","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/jasons-farewell\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/u73tyf0fa8v1/6SK2guLFYLH8FnhJtNxmJG/ec236ccbdceca9697879a22073264d5e/worldofdarkness-top_bg_free_content.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=630&amp;fit=fill&amp;f=center\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/jasons-farewell\" target=\"_blank\"> A Note from Jason Carl - Paradox Interactive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/jasons-farewell\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/jasons-farewell </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> World of Darkness </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After ten unforgettable years with White Wolf, the World of Darkness, and Paradox Interactive, I\u2019m saying farewell. Not as a goodbye, but as the close of one extraordinary chapter in an ongoing story.<br /> <br /> Working on <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> and the greater World of Darkness has been more than a job or a profession for me. It has been a calling, a privilege, and a creative responsibility I\u2019ve cherished deeply. Together with this remarkable community of fans, storytellers, and creators, I\u2019ve had the honor of helping rekindle a mythos that continues to inspire imagination and reflection across generations.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m most proud of is not just the stories we told, but the voices we welcomed. From the publication of Vampire 5th Edition to the introduction of the Storytellers Vault program; and from the very first episode of <i>LA by Night</i> to the resurrection of White Wolf at this year\u2019s <i>Darkness Emergent</i> celebration, it\u2019s been a joy to see new creators bring their own perspectives and passions into the night. The World of Darkness has always been strongest when it belongs to many, and I believe its best is still to come.<br /> <br /> Under the stewardship of Executive Vice President Marco Behrmann, Creative Director Jess Lanzillo, and the extraordinary creative team now shaping the future of the brand (you\u2019ll meet them all soon!), I have absolute confidence that the World of Darkness will continue to thrive, evolve, and surprise us all. Their creativity, passion, empathy, and ambition embody everything that first drew me to this world.<br /> <br /> To everyone who has been part of this journey - the fans, the collaborators, the dreamers who dared to make the darkness beautiful - thank you. You\u2019ve given me more than I can ever express, and far more than I can ever repay.<br /> <br /> Like all stories, our lives are told in chapters. And as this chapter closes, another begins. I\u2019ll be joining <b>Tabletop Vacations</b>, the creators of <a href=\"https://dndinacastle.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><u>D&amp;D in a Castle</u></b></a>, as the Dean of <a href=\"https://dndinacastle.com/products/dmu\" target=\"_blank\"><b><u>Dungeon Master University</u></b></a>, a place where Dungeon Masters gather to level up their craft, shape worlds, and kindle the spark of imagination. It is a new realm, but the same calling: to guide, to share, and to help others build their own stories, together.<br /> <br /> And there are, of course, more stories to be told, waiting for us, out there, somewhere, in the night. The World of Darkness will always be a part of me, and I carry it with me into every story I tell. Wherever I go, wherever the night leads, this world, its storytellers, and its beautiful monsters, endure.<br /> <br /> <b>Jason Carl</b><br /> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's the fallout of Bloodlines 2 or not but it seems that a shake up in White Wolf's structure is coming sooner than we thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T20:44:49-08:00","id":1556423,"title":"","content":"He doesn\u2019t sound unhappy about leaving. Sounds like he left on good terms and just found a better job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T01:51:45-08:00","id":1556425,"title":"","content":"Part of me is a bit cynical because Carl is an extremely skilled professional communicator and we'd never know based on his statement about leaving if it was truly amicable or if he's decided not burning bridges is more important than any grievance he might have with the higher-ups at Paradox.<br /> <br /> That said? Ultimately it doesn't really matter either way. Of the people with proven track records of knowing how to put out quality TTRPG books before getting hired by Paradox (not counting license partners), he was with them the longest; which means he actually had time to learn Paradox's internal culture to mesh it with his established industry know-how. While Behrmann and Lanzillo have the bone fides to run a TTRPG division of a company, the WoD isn't in a great spot right now and giving them time to settle in properly could make it even harder to start getting some serious wins for the franchise when it desperately needs some. Having Carl there would have been a big help for trying to right the ship. Lanzillo in particular is relatively new to Paradox (they hired her earlier this year), and I presume they're hoping she's got some ideas for getting the IPs singing. I also doubt they managed to sway her away from her old position at WotC on purely financial incentives. It feels like there's a huge risk that just like Achilli's tenure with the WoD, there's a risk of another person coming in, putting their stamp on the direction of the franchise, it not working out as long as it really needs to, that person leaves, and books feel disconnected from a lack of continuity in creative vision. Carl could have certainly been a good person to keep around to help avoid that if Paradox could have swung it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T18:21:05-08:00","id":1556453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1556421-brand-manger-jason-carl-just-left-white-wolf?p=1556423#post1556423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn\u2019t sound unhappy about leaving. Sounds like he left on good terms and just found a better job.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the letter of a good communicator in a page that belongs to the very corporation they left. It means nothing by itself.<br /> <br /> What I think was relevant was the next step, D&amp;D In a Castle and DMU. They're insanely expensive events, with D&amp;D IaC being exactly what it says on the tin. Being part of their permanent staff is quite a change of career, but I don't know how well they pay. It does look like a passion change more than just a falling with the previous employer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T20:00:59-08:00","id":1556459,"title":"","content":"He does have a background in being a producer for LARPs, and worked on the BNS run of MET books before moving to nWW/Paradox. With the YouTube AP he did as well, I wouldn't be surprised if he'd rather be back in the more in-depth play experiences side of things instead of brand management. While I doubt Paradox would have been upset if he did more YouTube stuff on his own time and dime, they don't seem inclined to do more to support that side of the WoD stuff despite the strength it had in LARP and related playstyles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T18:02:34-08:00","id":1556490,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's what really makes me believe the story has at least some truth. Even if there is some bad blood, it doesn't seems to be the main cause of his leaving.<br /> <br /> And for whatever Paradox could do to make it happen in their backyard now, the current situation made it pretty clear they're not going to increase expenses significantly in this area, no matter what. And as I said before, I can't blame them given their pattern of failing and repeating without learning anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T05:21:13-08:00","id":1556514,"title":"","content":"I'm also leaning more towards him simply choosing to leave because he likes the idea of doing that D&amp;D-thing more. He probably did introduce quite a few people to WOD5E with his Youtube Actual Plays. That certainly will be missed.<br /> <br /> But the same as with Justin Achilli, it's strange how when these people leave, there's no immediate hand-over and sense of continuation. This choice wasn't made overnight, I imagine. Yet again, though, a very senior figure leaves... and that's it. Like, okay, Jason Carl left. So who's the WOD-brand-manager at the new White Wolf right now? Why isn't there a statement from Jason Carl <i>as well as</i> the new White Wolf? When he says &quot;you\u2019ll meet them all soon!&quot;, my first thought was &quot;But why haven't we met them yet?&quot;. I know what the plan for Renegade looks like. Why can't we know what the revived White Wolf's plan for 2026 looks like? <br /> <br /> It's also awkward in that similar to how Justin Achilli had been a very public-facing figure for WOD when he worked for Paradox, when White Wolf was revived, it was Jason Carl who did most of the interviews about it. But now, once again, one of those figures who has been very central in talking with the public has left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T17:38:28-08:00","id":1556544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1556421-brand-manger-jason-carl-just-left-white-wolf?p=1556514#post1556514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also leaning more towards him simply choosing to leave because he likes the idea of doing that D&amp;D-thing more. He probably did introduce quite a few people to WOD5E with his Youtube Actual Plays. That certainly will be missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, those are big hands-on events where you meet a lot of players and DMs from around the world (though mostly the US, I guess), and do so in a nice place (D&amp;DIaC is literally run in a castle for real). For someone who likes to be with the community and doing the play part of the job, that's a great opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1556421-brand-manger-jason-carl-just-left-white-wolf?p=1556514#post1556514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the same as with Justin Achilli, it's strange how when these people leave, there's no immediate hand-over and sense of continuation. This choice wasn't made overnight, I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a huge problem.<br /> <br /> Of course, Paradox has a tendency of wanting to keep the suspense even on matters where this doesn't make sense, but it doesn't change that it doesn't make sense in such matters. But it does seem like they have nothing prepared for this when they definitely should have.<br /> <br /> But well, this is their small change sector, so it isn't like this will affect their costs or profits in any meaningful way, as bad as it is for us.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}